ntage lies in the fact that  this bishop is very active  very powerful and the black king even  with so few pieces on the board  is never going to be safe as long as  this bishop exists  and that's what we see happen we get b  takes c4  and now e4 by nepo just cements this  bishop in the center of the board  and this king will have no shelter so  long as this bishop lives  uh queen takes b2 by alexsenko might as  well grab some pawns you know die with  the full stomach  uh queen hhh check king e7 now queen c8  and nepo just dancing  on the light squares creating threats  all over the place  uh queen b6 is trying to hold on but now  queen takes c4  nepo again just up a clean pawn f7 is  hanging  and the king is getting checkmated queen  to b5  we now see the check and queen c5 and at  this point alexenko had seen enough  went ahead and resigned the game of  course if you play queen d6  you're gonna get checked again and white  can simply pick up the pawn  race this guy up the board and continue  making threats around the black king  and with this game nepo pulled into  clear  well was already in clear first but  extended his lead in clear first place  staying just a little bit ahead of a  niche geary  right up until the very end so great  game  by nepo and hopefully we all learned a  little something  about why the catalan can be so  dangerous and so scary  that's all i have for you guys today  thank you so much for watching and as  always i will see you  next time

